king for  facts yeah so is so are your colleagues  on Capitol Hill but they're being denied  access to the whistleblowers compliant  no they asked to handle this in the  appropriate manner that it's supposed to  just as the law says if he goes to the  inspector general which goes to the  inside the intelligence community yeah  normally in other cases the  whistleblower can come to Congress but  in an Intel community it can go to the  the inspector general would then go to  the to the DNI that a Director of  National Intelligence the Acting  Director McGuire he's handling this now  he's coming before Congress in a public  hearing of the Intel committee next  Thursday that's the appropriate way to  handle instead of leaking or putting  something out because they want to turn  the story to be different just like the  New York Times did last week you heard  the Rudy Giuliani back and forth about  no I didn't yes I did  ash the Ukrainians to investigate there  is a story here the New York Times that  the president goes after a lot did a  very big story about hunter Biden  working for this oligarch in a Oil  Company and and all of this background  to this investigation and there's their  there the reporters say there's more to  come  and what's your point that my point is  in in Joe Biden's own words he tells how  he pressured the Ukraine government that  they would not get funding from America  unless they fired a prosecutor it's  concerning to me is that prosecutor  investigating his son and he said you've  got six hours and within six hours they  fired him and Jill Bryan was proud of it  I've only learned to this by Joe Biden  telling us about it so you think the DNI  is going to come forward with  information I'm real concerned about  that and would it be interesting  politically if you wanted people not to  look at what Biden was doing to try to  bring something once again alleged  against this president as they've done  time and again because they do not like  an ou